curity to detain individuals who are in the country without authorization and have been arrested for or charged with burglary, theft, larceny, or shoplifting. It would also allow state governments to sue the federal government for injunctive relief when federal immigration enforcement decisions or failures—such as releasing individuals from custody or not fulfilling visa or asylum processing requirements—cause harm to the state or its residents, including financial harm exceeding $100.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People applying to live here, and their families here. People applying to come here, and their families here.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"S000250","score":0.02595346470272257},"overlapCount":50},"meaning":{"percentile":14.452693097456958,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7093586824790074}},{"billId":"119-hr-5334","bioguideId":"B001327","cycle":2026,"score":0.002748185133653434,"matches":[{"industry":"education","donorAmount":9000,"donorShare":0.002748185133653434,"billConfidence":0.95,"contribution":0.002748185133653434}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7093586824790074},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-5334","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"5334","title":"SEED Act","introducedDate":"2025-09-11","latestActionDate":"2026-07-23","latestActionText":"Cloture motion on the motion to proceed to the measure presented in Senate. (CR S4253)","policyArea":"Taxation","subjects":["Income tax deductions","Preschool education","Teaching, teachers, curricula"],"sponsorBioguideId":"P000613","cosponsorCount":23,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5334","industries":[{"industry":"education","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"The bill directly affects early childhood education providers by changing the tax treatment of their employees' expenses."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would allow early childhood educators (pre-kindergarten teachers and staff) to claim the same federal tax deduction for unreimbursed classroom and professional development expenses that is currently available only to kindergarten through grade 12 educators. The deduction is capped at $300 in 2025 and adjusts annually for inflation. It would reduce taxable income for eligible early childhood educators who pay out-of-pocket for supplies and training.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who files a tax return. Anyone who pays federal tax.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"T000487","score":0.03645189751853493},"overlapCount":24},"meaning":{"percentile":12.494076765123992,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7093586824790074}}],"votes":[{"id":"a64a90b759595d68f3a8d502","billId":"119-hr-7008","date":"2026-07-22T16:51:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll280.xml"},{"id":"2afa499bcaceefdcecfa862a","billId":"119-hr-8800","date":"2026-07-22T16:37:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll278.xml"},{"id":"e69a4fe10a0cc4e4d35ffc3d","billId":"119-hr-6955","date":"2026-07-21T22:05:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll271.xml"},{"id":"c68077c5b6dd6fe8eb42bf43","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:39:00-04:00","question":"Recorded Vote","result":"Passed","position":"Aye","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll254.xml"},{"id":"3944446cfd7ceaa28fbc0515","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:11:00-04:00","ques